CICADAS scream beneath a white-hot sky. A modern Japanese city swelters. A/C UNITS HUM. Electric fans spin behind storefronts. Cars crawl through traffic, anime characters plastered across their doors, pop music rattling from open windows. A VENDING MACHINE drops a bottle of green tea into a sweating OFFICE WORKER'S hands. POK\u201\'c9MON and DIGIMON displays compete for window space. A TOYOTA ad hangs above a HONDA showroom. A MITSUBISHI BOX TRUCK crawls through traffic. Elsewhere, women in KIMONO head toward a summer festival. TEENAGERS IN COSPLAY go the opposite way. Even the dogs have surrendered to the heat. Through it all walks HIROSHI TAKAHASHI, 95, relaxed and formally dressed. His back is bent despite his effort to straighten it. A small bag hangs from his shoulder. Ahead: DAITOKU-JI TEMPLE COMPLEX. Ancient wood and stone surrounded by the modern city. At the gate, a BOY waits in the shade, copper-skinned, backpack over one shoulder. Sweat pours down his face. Hiroshi looks him over.}
