The Boy gets to work. Water darkens the grave stones. Fresh SHIKIMI replaces the old. Leaves are swept away. Incense prepared. Hiroshi watches. His attention settles on the inscriptions. Names. Dates. 1939. 1940. 1941. 1942. 1943. Another 1945. And another. Some names are beautifully carved. Others look hurried. Almost slapped into stone. Hiroshi's face tightens. Beside them, newer memorial stones preserve photographs beneath protective covers. Young faces. Hiroshi stares at them. Then notices something else. His sorrow hardens. A newer marker: REIA TAKAHASHI}
